# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Zheyong Fan et al. (2022). GPUMD: A package for constructing accurate machine-learned potentials and performing highly efficient atomistic simulations.
#   The Journal of Chemical Physics. doi:10.1063/5.0106617  arXiv:2205.10046v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2205.10046v2 (sha256 55cb9c2a457852b3...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 250 (Software/implementation). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/fan2022.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the NEP2 and NEP3 models for the MgAlCu alloy (Table I)
# and the carbon comparison of Table II (NEP3 at two cutoffs against DP,
# GAP, MTP and REANN, with RMSEs on the 450-structure test set and the MD
# speed of each potential). The silicon and azobenzene comparisons (Figs. 4
# and 5, figure-only values), the active-learning study (Fig. 9), the
# diamond properties of Table III and the heat-transport applications are
# not encoded.

