###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Table II gives the MD speed (atom-steps per ms) for a diamond cell at
# 300 K: DP (compressed), REANN and NEP on one 32-GB Tesla V100 GPU, GAP and
# MTP on 72 Intel Xeon-Gold 6240 cores; per-atom times are 1000/speed. NEP3
# on one Tesla A100 reaches about 1.5e7 atom-steps per second. The maximum
# number of atoms on one V100 (Nmax: 240e3 and 220e3 for DP, 4,100e3 and
# 5,800e3 for NEP, 290e3, 180e3 and 64e3 for REANN) is not encoded. No
# training times are given.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - NEP2 and NEP3 are versions of the registry method NEP (fan2021): NEP3 changes the radial functions to linear combinations of Chebyshev basis functions and adds four- and five-body angular descriptor components; both are encoded as runs of NEP.
# - Virial RMSEs (meV/atom; Table I and Table II) have no metric property in the schema and are not encoded. The GAP RMSEs of Table II are taken from Ref. [10]; this paper does not train the GAP model, so no training data set is attached to it. Its SOAP n_max = l_max = 8 is not encoded.
# - NEP radial/angular basis sizes (n_max, N_bas, l_max), the population size and the regularisation weights have no hyperparameter individual; DP network sizes, learning-rate schedules and loss weights, and the REANN network sizes are not encoded.
# - Silicon (Fig. 4) and azobenzene/rMD17 (Fig. 5) accuracy-versus-cost comparisons are given only as figures and are not encoded; Table III elastic constants and lattice constant of diamond are properties, not error metrics, and are not encoded.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/fan2022.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

# --- BenchmarkResult labels (generated by artifacts/scripts/add_result_labels.py; do not edit) ---
